## Read, inspect, decide

The same **content**, *typography*, and `inline code` appear in every reference. Notice what draws your attention first: the prose, the syntax, or the surrounding interface.

```rust
// Preserve meaning, even when the colors change.
struct Sample { name: String, score: f32 }

fn select(samples: &[Sample], minimum: f32) -> Vec<&Sample> {
    samples.iter()
        .filter(|sample| sample.score >= minimum)
        .collect()
}

let label = "A warmer environment, the same code";
let enabled = true;
```

A quiet appearance can use **fewer color groups** or **less chroma**. Those are different edits. A [link](https://example.com) should remain identifiable without taking over the paragraph.
